@startuml langgraph-agent-graph
' The LangGraph StateGraph for the agent mode (ADR-046), the default
' orchestrator. Nodes call the same domain ports as the hand-rolled loop
' (ADR-030) — policy, search provider, critic, step reporter — so the domain
' stays framework-free. State is checkpointed to Redis (keyed by job_id) at
' every super-step, so an interrupt() pause resumes mid-graph instead of
' re-running the searches already done.

hide empty description

state decide : policy.decide(goal, journal, hits)\nthe LLM picks the next action
state search : provider.search(query)\ndedup by canonical URL, keep new hits\njournal «search» (query, reason, new_hits)
state ask : interrupt(question)\npause for the user (HITL, ADR-032)
state finalize : journal «finish» (reason)
state critique : critic.critique(goal, hits) — ADR-031\ndrop off-topic, one repair search if budget left\njournal «critique» (assessment)

[*] --> decide : invoke({goal})\n**or** Command(resume=answer)

decide --> search : action = search
decide --> ask : action = ask\n(goal ambiguous, no clarification yet\nAND a clarifier is wired)
decide --> finalize : action = finish\n**or** step budget spent\n**or** spend cap hit (ADR-048)

search --> decide : back to the policy\nwith the growing transcript
ask --> decide : on resume: answer folded into the goal,\nasked = true (one question per job)

finalize --> critique
critique --> [*]

note right of ask
  **interrupt() = the pause.** The worker sees the
  interrupt, fires POST /internal/jobs/{id}/question
  once (job -> awaiting_input) and the task ends.
  The user's answer re-dispatches a task that resumes
  **this** graph from its Redis checkpoint — the
  searches done before the pause are not redone.
end note

note bottom of decide
  **Durable checkpoint** after every super-step:
  Redis, keyed by job_id (ADR-046). The checkpointed
  state holds JSON primitives only (hits/steps as
  dicts) — no pickling of domain dataclasses.
end note

note bottom of critique
  After END the worker runs the **shared tail** (as in
  the workflow mode): batched enrichment (ADR-042),
  sort by date, flag the recurring delta (ADR-033),
  then deliver — POST /internal/jobs/{id}/results.
end note

@enduml
